A||||6||FieroMike||ADS Chip/ Fiero Store||||||
Z||000000||FieroMike||04-12-99||11:33 AM||||Has anyone istalled the ADS chip from the Fiero Store?  Anybody get dynoed before and after.  I think this is the first mod that I am going to do, so just wondering.  If not, I will post the results, I plan on getting it in about 3 weeks.
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||04-12-99||02:44 PM||||I'm curious about the results also. I've read a lot of different stories about all these performance chips. Some say they had gotten a noticable increase in performance, others say it didn't do anything. So please keep us updated.
Z||000002||Shaun41178||04-12-99||11:12 PM||||FieroMike, I really suggest that you don't spend your money on a computer chip.  There is a dyno shop about an hour away from my house and I met with another Fiero owner who purchased an ADS chip and a Hypertech chip.  Both chips were dynoed and niether chip gave any significant hp increase.  I saw the dyno charts myself.  In fact the chip increased the timing so much the base timing had to be retarded back to 6 degrees BTDC.  The most increase that the chip gave was 1, maybe 2 hp tops and 1-2 pound feet of torque tops.  <p>Plus you have to run premium fuel all the time which also adds up when these chips are used.  Please take my word for it that these chips do not add any power.  You will not "feel" any difference because there will be no difference.  The only difference will be a lighter wallet.  <p>I suggest doing proven Hot Rod techniques to give you more power.  Such as porting, polishing, installing high lift cam, high flow cat and good cat-back.  These mods can add up to 30 hp or so with the cam and porting adding the most.<p>One easy mod you can do is to port your exhaust manifolds.  I just finished with mine.  Total cost was about $11.  I had an extra set and after pulling off the un-ported ones I compared them to the ones that I ported and there was a BIG difference in the amount that the manifolds can flow now.  I am guessing that I got around 8-10 hp from doing this mod.  Even with this increase I could still not "feel" any difference in the acceleration of the car.  However it revs a lot cleaner now and idles smoother and the engine compartment seems to run a tad bit cooler.  I have baselined my car on the dyno and I plan to get back in the next couple of weeks to see how much of an increase I got.  I baselined at 128 at the wheels in case anyone cares and that is with no mods.  I am now expecting around 136-140.
Z||000003||Pretender||04-13-99||12:05 AM||||i have installed the ads superchip in my 88gt, i can feel the difference, on sat. i will be visiting the local track to see how much improvement it made. Personally i would reccomend it but thats just me, maybe my factory chip was falty and i just restored it back to normal by adding the chip, anyways sat. is the day of proof., i'll keep you guys informed.
Z||000005||Pretender||08-08-99||03:44 AM||||I've gained 4 tenths in the 1/4 mile from adding the power pully and chip!...take my word for it too.
Z||000007||Bruce||08-08-99||08:03 PM||||I added the ADS chip, and it seemed to make the car run smoother (I'm not into the speed mode). I'm going back and forth about buying and installing headers. After all is said and done with the stock manifolds, I don't see much difference in the cost to port and polish the present ones or add headers from West Coast Fieros. I don't do any mechaincal work, other than oil changes and the basics, so I'm not sure about the installation $, etc.<br>Any hints or advice?
Z||000008||WisconsinGT||08-08-99||09:41 PM||||Yeah Bruce, I am in the same boat as you. I am glad to see that I am not the only one who can only handle the basics.<p>Regarding the header issue. I just received two excellent used stock manafolds from Ed Parks. He did the reinforced welding work. Now I have to grind out the ports. (or have someone else do it.) I too, was going to do the header thing, but decided that all I want is a good running car with minimal fuss. After reading other post on this issue, I thought that working with the factory manafolds will satisfy my needs. I also thought about putting a new cam in as well. My take on adding performance is that my gas milage will suffer. So I gave it a miss as well. Anyway, do what you think is best for your needs.
